 {"id":"fabro-03ef","title":"lab: migrate develop+revisor run behavior from project.toml to workflow.toml (v0.345 intent runs stop transmitting project settings)","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T20:31:01.034Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T21:31:27.428Z","description":"Migrate develop + revisor run behavior from denkhaus-lab project.toml into each workflow's own workflow.toml, required by upstream v0.345.0-nightly.0 (merge 6530c724f): `fabro run`/`fabro create` create runs from immutable workflow intents and no longer transmit project-level `[run]`+`[environments]` settings (warning only). Until this lands, every manual develop/revisor start silently runs on the server `default` environment (buildpack-deps:noble, 2 CPU/4 GB, no toolchain), skips mise/bootstrap prepare, falls back to a non-glm-5.3 default model, skips branch pushes, opens NO pull request (breaks the autonomous merge-back dev cycle), and posts no Slack terminal notifications.\n\nChange set (on branch denkhaus-lab):\n1. develop + revisor workflow.toml: add `[run.environment] id=\"mise\"`, `[run.prepare]` (mise install, just bootstrap), `[run.model]` (zai glm-5.3), `[run.run_branch]`/`[run.meta_branch]` push=true, `[run.pull_request]` (enabled, auto_merge, squash, titler zai:glm-4.7), `[run.integrations.github.permissions]` (contents/pull_requests write), `[run.notifications.terminal]` (slack #dev-fabro). All keys verified workflow-transmissible in RunLayer (lib/foundation/fabro-config/src/layers/run.rs); admission applies the workflow layer at intent compilation.\n2. Start wrapper: manual starts MUST pass `--environment mise` — the intent's environment override sits above the workflow layer, so a workflow-level pin alone does not select it (run_intent.rs admission + create.rs default to DEFAULT_ENVIRONMENT_ID). Pin it in the lab start script/just recipe so it cannot be forgotten.\n3. Slim project.toml run keys on denkhaus-lab afterwards (they are inert for CLI runs now; only produce the warning).\n4. Placement stays server-managed: the deployed server already carries the `mise` environment (fabro-runner:mise, 8 CPU/16 GB) — no environment creation needed.\n\nOrdering: do this BEFORE the two revisor qualification cycles of ADR-0013/fabro-5453 — broken merge-back would pollute the loop measurement.\n\nVerification: one manual `fabro run develop --environment mise` from a lab checkout that (a) shows the untransmitted-settings warning ONLY for remaining project keys (ideally none), (b) runs with the mise image and glm-5.3, (c) executes prepare steps, (d) opens and auto-merges its PR, (e) posts the terminal Slack notification.","blocks":["fabro-5453"],"closedAt":"2026-09-03T21:31:27.428Z","closeReason":"Qualified green on run 01M1MHGS7PH26EP20B2RTAPN4G (2026-09-03): mise environment (sandbox 1s, prepare 2 cmds/16s), glm-5.3 from workflow.toml, no untransmitted-settings warning, PR #12 created and auto-merged (squash, wrapper ff-pull), notifications settings proven in spec with zero failure/skip logs. Two full cycles, BOTH fib seeds (fabro-93f2 -step, fabro-87cf -last) implemented, gated, approved first-pass, closed; lab tracker 0 open. 10.3 min, $0.68. Non-blocker: PR content fell back deterministically (fabro-cd27)."}
 {"id":"fabro-2e73","title":"fabro checkout: manual `fabro run implement-issue` needs --environment toolchain since v0.345 intent runs","status":"open","type":"task","priority":3,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T20:31:07.317Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T20:31:23.727Z","description":"Since upstream v0.345.0-nightly.0 (merge 6530c724f), manual `fabro run`/`fabro create` no longer transmit project-level [run]/[environments] settings. In the fabro checkout, .fabro/project.toml pins [run.environment] id=\"toolchain\" (rust/bun/sd/ml toolchain image fabro-toolchain:noble) — a manual `fabro run implement-issue` (whose workflow.toml carries no environment) now silently falls back to the server `default` environment (buildpack-deps:noble, no toolchain) with only a warning. Fix: either add [run.environment] id=\"toolchain\" to implement-issue/workflow.toml for documentation + workflow-owned fields AND pass --environment toolchain at start (intent override outranks the workflow pin), or wrap the manual start in a just recipe that passes the flag. Server already exposes the toolchain environment (8 CPU/16 GB). Low priority: implement-issue is currently triggered manually only."}
 {"id":"fabro-4398","title":"gofib tests: replace per-flag opts() wrappers with one options-literal builder","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T21:49:30.902Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T21:49:36.429Z","description":"From run 01M1MHGS7PH26EP20B2RTAPN4G (implementer@3 observation): fib_test.go predates the newer flags (-step, -last); every flag combination needed its own opts wrapper (stepOpts, lastOpts, ...), and each future flag would add another. Composing flags in tests drifts toward wrapper soup.\n\nRefactor: ONE test helper that takes an options literal (or builder) defaulting to the current defaults (n=100, start=0, limit=0, seed=0, step=1, last=0, format unset, json/pretty/sum/version false, output empty) and overrides only what a test exercises. All existing tests migrate to it; the per-flag wrappers are deleted.\n\nAcceptance: (1) exactly ONE options-construction helper remains in fib_test.go; (2) no test constructs options{} literals inline except through the helper; (3) behavior-neutral — the full test suite passes unchanged assertions; (4) just qualitygate stays green.","closedAt":"2026-09-03T21:49:36.429Z","closeReason":"Filed on the wrong tracker (platform); fib product seeds live on the lab branch — recreated there."}
-{"id":"fabro-f677","title":"engine: preamble context table breaks markdown with multi-line values","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":3,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T22:16:01.052Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T22:16:01.052Z","description":"The `## Current context` table (append_filtered_context_table, summary:high fidelity) inlines multi-line values raw into markdown table cells. Markdown tables cannot contain newlines, so every renderer breaks: rows after a multi-line value visually detach from the table. User report 2026-09-03, run 01M1MMK5C6B313SY70Y2EPKE82 implementer@1: current_seed_id and current_seed_title appeared \"missing\" because the multi-line current_seed_brief (acceptance bullet list) shattered the table around them.\n\nFix directions (pick one or combine):\n1. Render multi-line values single-line (newlines -> \" / \") in table cells; full value stays available via the context_read tool.\n2. Emit long/multi-line values as a bullet list BELOW the table (compact-fidelity style) with a short first-line cell + pointer.\n3. Extend the existing large-value demote path to also trigger on newline count, not just byte size, so blob-ref handling applies.\n\nAcceptance: (1) a context value containing newlines renders as a valid single table row per key in every markdown viewer (web UI prompt view included); (2) current_seed_id/title stay visually adjacent to a multi-line brief; (3) no information loss for agents (full value still served by context_read); (4) unit test with a multi-line context value asserting one rendered row per key."}
+{"id":"fabro-f677","title":"engine: preamble context table breaks markdown with multi-line values","status":"in_progress","type":"bug","priority":3,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T22:16:01.052Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-04T06:35:08.811Z","description":"The `## Current context` table (append_filtered_context_table, summary:high fidelity) inlines multi-line values raw into markdown table cells. Markdown tables cannot contain newlines, so every renderer breaks: rows after a multi-line value visually detach from the table. User report 2026-09-03, run 01M1MMK5C6B313SY70Y2EPKE82 implementer@1: current_seed_id and current_seed_title appeared \"missing\" because the multi-line current_seed_brief (acceptance bullet list) shattered the table around them.\n\nFix directions (pick one or combine):\n1. Render multi-line values single-line (newlines -> \" / \") in table cells; full value stays available via the context_read tool.\n2. Emit long/multi-line values as a bullet list BELOW the table (compact-fidelity style) with a short first-line cell + pointer.\n3. Extend the existing large-value demote path to also trigger on newline count, not just byte size, so blob-ref handling applies.\n\nAcceptance: (1) a context value containing newlines renders as a valid single table row per key in every markdown viewer (web UI prompt view included); (2) current_seed_id/title stay visually adjacent to a multi-line brief; (3) no information loss for agents (full value still served by context_read); (4) unit test with a multi-line context value asserting one rendered row per key."}
